WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:44.280
Let me give this to you straight...

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.280
What kind of a man does that to his own son?

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.080
Elliot Hope is not a racist.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:52.520
He's got family problems.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.800
That's no excuse!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:55.320
James, I...

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.480
I've got to go.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.840
He called the wedding off...

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.400
Becky, we need to find him.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:03.640
Thandie Abebe is incompetent.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:09.040
I take full responsibility.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.120
How many times must she screw up?

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.920
They make a lovely couple, don't they?

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.800
How long have you known?

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:05.800
Your father contacted our solicitor...

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.720
MY solicitor!

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.560
..Three weeks ago.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:12.880
Hoped for a "clean break".

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.800
Positively surgical, don't you think?

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:22.160
A sharp knife and a steady hand and it's as if 30 years never existed.

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:24.280
Why didn't you tell me?

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:28.360
I do have a little pride left, darling.

00:02:27.440 --> 00:02:28.600
Or I did.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.640
It's all so undignified.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.120
For all of us.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.920
I'm going to talk to him.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.720
No, please don't.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:36.520
MOBILE PHONE BEEPS He's making a mistake.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:40.920
Ah, I think, nowadays, I'm the mistake.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.080
These thing happen, darling.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.120
We just have to cope with them.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.480
Don't talk to him.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:55.320
No work?

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:01.480
No work, no cases, no admissions, no nothing.

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:05.560
Remind me, why did I agree to do a shift on Darwin?

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:08.920
Boredom is God's gift to the over-stimulated.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.120
I advise you to revel in it.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:13.440
Taking some of your own advice?

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.040
Background reading.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.320
My racial awareness course.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:23.360
Well, you can always make an excuse, I don't know, erm, someone needs a heart transplant, that kind of thing.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.600
The wise man follows the path of least resistance.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.560
Even if it's a waste of time?

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.280
Ah, you must be the early bird.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.480
And what does that make you?

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.840
Latest minutes from the board.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:38.640
Funding, new central initiatives.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:38.800
All hot stuff.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:40.360
Isn't it always?

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:43.840
Ahh...the awareness course.

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.440
It's today, isn't it?

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:47.120
Dr Miranda's a friend of mine.

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:51.440
I knew her at Johns Hopkins.

00:03:50.560 --> 00:03:54.240
She's what you'd call a dynamic woman.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.560
Oh, my favourite kind.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:04:00.480
It's a shame we couldn't come to a more equitable arrangement.

00:03:59.760 --> 00:04:01.160
Race is such a hot potato.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.760
Heads have rolled because of it.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.520
Big ones.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:05.800
Guess who's knitting by the guillotine.

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:08.240
Do this for me and we can all get back to the important stuff.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.120
Enjoy.

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:11.960
Enjoy.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.000
You don't think you could be overreacting?

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:21.480
Abra has done everything to undermine me.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:24.640
Or there was a misunderstanding.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:28.600
You can't afford bad blood in the department.

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:30.400
Last week, you were on my side.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:30.720
I am.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:36.120
But accusations, mud slinging - it never pays in the long run.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.160
So you think I should apologise?

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.240
Maybe go down on my knees?

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:41.480
Would that make you happy?

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:45.840
All I'm suggesting is that you just meet Abra half way.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:48.920
Swallow some of that pride.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.400
Pride?

00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.080
You never know who's watching.

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:53.160
OK.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:55.280
I give up.

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.480
Where have you hidden them?

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:58.320
We've got a visitor.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.720
Hmm.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.520
Morning.

00:05:05.960 --> 00:05:08.240
My day on the floor.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.360
Once a month, whether I like it or not.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.120
And we got lucky.

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:16.440
What are the chances?

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.240
Fair to middling, I'd say.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:25.720
But will you like what you see?

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:27.280
Shall we?

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:30.960
To paraphrase someone or other, AAU is another country.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.560
We do things differently here.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.000
..

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.200
Still on Africa time, Dr Abebe?

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.960
As I was saying, this is our rapid assessment bay.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.600
Obs, bloods, initial investigations all happen here.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:44.040
15 minutes max, then it's decision time.

00:05:43.200 --> 00:05:48.760
Anything to add, Mr Griffin?

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.200
Just that we're all behind you.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:51.520
It's a great initiative.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.480
A real team effort.

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.080
If you'll excuse me.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:01.840
The punter, or do you prefer client?

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:03.960
What about patient?

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:04.440
Ooh.

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:12.440
He or she is then either referred on or transferred to one of our treatment areas, freeing the bay for the next one.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.400
It's all pretty simple really.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.160
It sounds it.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:19.200
I can't wait to see it in action.

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:19.440
You will.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.440
I mean, er... it's never usually this quiet.

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:22.680
Oh!

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:23.440
She said the Q word.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.760
We never say the Q word.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.280
Saying the Q word brings the world down on our heads.

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:29.560
The disco spin is the only known cure.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:33.680
You did that, because I said quiet?

00:06:32.720 --> 00:06:34.160
Oh, dear.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.600
Though the power of the spin is strictly limited.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:38.440
So please don't say it again.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.280
For all our sakes.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:50.240
Apparently, my ulcer also disapproves of divorce.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.600
Joseph, I...

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:56.600
I understand how difficult this must be for you.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:07:06.080
Believe me, and I assure you I would not have entered into it unless it was something extremely important to me.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:06.840
Clearly.

00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:09.160
If it's worth destroying our family for.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:12.360
That was never my intention.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.720
I suppose I just hoped you might understand.

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:16.120
Well, a dalliance, maybe.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:19.760
But divorce?

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.080
My feelings have grown.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:22.080
Slowly, but surely.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.280
As have hers.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:30.840
And if Jac is to step into Diane's shoes, then we all have to come to some agreement.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:33.560
She's replacing Diane?

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:36.280
I thought the board decided not to appoint.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.120
It was a change of heart.

00:07:36.360 --> 00:07:39.280
I see.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.520
And yet you still trust her motives?

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:48.200
Should I have any reason not to?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:49.560
Yes, yes.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:49.720
I remember those were my thoughts exactly.

00:07:48.840 --> 00:07:51.160
What's she really doing here?

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:54.440
Checking up, snooping around, take your pick.

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:57.760
Question is, who tipped her off?

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:00.760
I'll give you one guess.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:05.240
For once, I think we're in total agreement.

00:08:04.320 --> 00:08:05.440
She seems all right, though.

00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:07.600
For a CEO.

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:07.880
Oh, no.

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:10.200
Classic smiling death.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:14.720
You don't see the knife till there's blood on the floor.

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:17.200
Don't you think that's just a little bit paranoid?

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:20.160
Oh, so you haven't heard the story?

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.080
She sacked her own father?

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:25.080
It was a family firm.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:26.840
She'd been to business school, he asked for her help.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:33.200
So darling Jayne restructured and decided Daddy was the weakest link.

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:34.039
Wow!

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:37.120
I think it was what they call a hostile takeover.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.679
Our system works.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:40.280
We've got nothing to worry about.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:47.400
Maybe, but if I want to persuade her to support the night ops, we need to be cooking with gas today.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:52.440
No slip ups, no mistakes, no surprises.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:55.640
Treatment room.

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:59.120
Can't you just remove it?

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:05.560
Mr Prince has a six-inch stiletto in his praecordium.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.480
It could be sitting in lung, pericardium, even myocardium...

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:09.600
Question is - how did it get there?

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:12.720
It was me.

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:12.960
I did it.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.520
Oh, it's not her fault.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.360
I asked her to.

00:09:14.840 --> 00:09:16.920
To stab you?

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:18.640
No, no.

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:18.920
We, er...

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:20.680
We have an arrangement.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:25.680
Geoff is my client.

00:09:24.760 --> 00:09:29.200
He likes to be walked on.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:29.560
It's my...my peccadillo.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:32.520
But obviously not your wife's?

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.840
It happens.

00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:34.520
Ask your husband.

00:09:33.560 --> 00:09:39.720
Right, I'll call theatres.

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:45.360
We're going to need eight of O neg, an echo and five sets of crossed fingers.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:45.720
So he's OK?

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:46.360
For a man with a shoe in his left ventricle, yes.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.720
She can stay with me, right?

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:52.520
If that's what you want?

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:53.080
Yeah.

00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:57.880
The hoards descend.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:58.280
Shall we see your famous system at a stretch?

00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.840
The Q word.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:02.800
Today of all days, someone had to say the Q word.

00:10:02.520 --> 00:10:03.760
It's groundless.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.120
You did a perfectly good operation.

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:09.560
She just ended up with a minor wound infection.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:14.600
The board will investigate, come to the same conclusions...

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.920
It's just a little unnerving.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.880
Yeah, well, it's part and parcel.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:22.960
If I had a penny for every time I'd had a complaint, I'd have...

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:23.480
How much?

00:10:22.920 --> 00:10:25.640
Three pence.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.080
Yes, that's not the best example.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:27.320
But anyway, we'll deal with it.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.480
So where are they off to this time, Margaret?

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:33.000
SHE PANTS Ibiza.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:33.360
Ooh!

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:35.840
All right for some, eh?

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:37.280
Yeah!

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.840
Tut-tut.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:42.600
Will you start the nebs and get a chest X-ray?

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.600
No problem.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:47.640
One of your regulars?

00:10:46.720 --> 00:10:51.320
Chronic Bronchitis.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:56.800
You do realise an acute medical bed costs this hospital £430 a day?

00:10:56.160 --> 00:10:59.640
We like to call it real life.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:04.880
So if I could place her?

00:11:04.000 --> 00:11:05.520
We would be forever in your debt.

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.640
Sounds like a challenge.

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:08.920
A bit like your other proposal.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:09.400
Operating at night?

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.240
It's certainly original.

00:11:09.800 --> 00:11:11.160
Yes, and necessary.

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:12.880
Have you seen the figures?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.480
I have read it.

00:11:12.520 --> 00:11:20.960
Doing it would mean staff operating after hours for no extra pay?

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:21.320
Yes, but...

00:11:20.520 --> 00:11:23.840
Takes quite a boss to inspire that kind of team spirit.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:27.880
Well... ..they're lucky they've got one, then.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:28.040
Excuse me.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:31.840
All I want is to be considered on my own merits.

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:36.120
And your determination to delay my morning list is duly noted.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:37.760
Here, catch this, file it.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:38.160
Oh, safe hands.

00:11:37.320 --> 00:11:40.720
Welcome to the first 15.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:44.440
But you do agree that we have to replace Diane?

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:50.640
Since when have the board taken any notice of my opinion?

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:51.040
I'll give you this back.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.200
But you're backing the creation of a new consultant's post?

00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:55.600
On clinical grounds if nothing else?

00:11:54.640 --> 00:12:02.120
Listen, I have a very flat back swing and no time to groove in the changes my pro is insisting on.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.520
Less time in theatre means more time on the range for yours truly.

00:12:01.640 --> 00:12:07.400
But I'd want my choice of candidates.

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:12.600
Which means this thing goes out country wide - it's a fair fight.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:15.360
And may the best man win.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.120
Or woman.

00:12:15.600 --> 00:12:16.800
Or indeed, woman.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:19.040
I've no idea what you mean.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.520
My father.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:25.000
When you've got Diane's job, let him down gently.

00:12:24.080 --> 00:12:25.240
You're just two different people, that sort of thing.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:29.400
Or will you have the guts to tell the truth?

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.200
Which is?

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:30.840
That you're using him to further your career.

00:12:29.960 --> 00:12:36.800
And as soon as you get what you want, you will move on and damn the consequences.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:38.640
Or perhaps I love him.

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:41.200
Same way you loved me?

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:45.800
Kris Turner.

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:50.120
Got hit on the nose playing basketball.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:53.120
He's tachy at 120.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:54.680
Airway?

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:57.200
HE GROANS He's maintaining it, just.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:57.560
Must be one hell of an elbow.

00:12:56.680 --> 00:12:59.200
It's just a nosebleed.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:13:02.000
So why isn't it stopping?

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:05.480
Because my brother's got haemophilia.

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:05.880
Ah!

00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:09.200
I will be right with you.

00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:17.080
Do you think an amateur with a flat back swing could ever win the British Open?

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:20.400
Do you think this... is an Open-winning action?

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.160
I would say almost certainly not, no.

00:13:21.440 --> 00:13:23.720
Gimme two seconds.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:27.040
I'm suppose I'm just nervous.

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:30.600
Afraid of a little competition?

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.080
Doesn't sound like you.

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:33.680
When something's this important.

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.000
The job means I can stay with you.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.600
It's all in hand.

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:36.840
My hands.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:38.480
I don't understand.

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:43.080
Ric Griffin needs a friend on the board.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:43.320
I want you in that job.

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:45.120
Quid Pro Quo.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:48.640
I can get this job on my own.

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.280
On my own merits.

00:13:48.400 --> 00:13:52.360
I don't doubt it, but this is just a little insurance.

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:53.080
For us, our future.

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:55.360
You said so yourself.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.360
I just want to make sure.

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:58.880
What about Clifford?

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:02.720
He won't accept a fait accompli.

00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:04.960
If he finds out we're together...

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.120
Leave Daniel Clifford to me.

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:05.240
There is something else I need to tell you.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:09.480
I've instructed my solicitor to take steps to... make our separation permanent.

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.000
You're getting a divorce?

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:18.920
Yes, I wanted to keep it quiet, but now Joseph knows, I thought you should hear it from me.

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:19.640
Please say something.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:22.400
It is a big step.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.160
But the right one.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:26.680
Like this, we don't have to hide anything.

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:27.880
Unless you'd prefer it that way?

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:28.400
I'd understand.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:35.480
In view of the potential conflict of interest as regards this job...

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:38.040
Oh, my God!

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:41.640
Some things are more important.

00:14:44.160 --> 00:14:50.400
Well, you can say what you like about this place, it's never dull.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.400
Er, sorry, you wanted to talk to me about something?

00:14:54.640 --> 00:14:55.680
No.

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.040
KNOCK ON DOOR Come.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.320
Thank you.

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:13.440
Curiouser and curiouser.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:17.360
Yes?

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:23.320
Mr Hope?

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.720
Speaking.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:26.240
It's DS Doyle.

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.800
DS Doyle.

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:28.800
We, er, have some news.

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:30.600
You've found him.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:31.880
Thank God.

00:15:31.520 --> 00:15:35.800
We need you to come down to the coroners office.

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:37.040
Stop that.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:45.680
I wasn't expecting her to announce it to the world.

00:15:45.320 --> 00:15:48.480
What's done is done.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:51.560
I did ask you not to interfere.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:56.360
Yes, and I'm sorry.

00:15:55.560 --> 00:15:57.360
So you keep saying.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:01.600
You did what you thought was right.

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:02.040
Still...

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:05.960
Now there's not much point in delaying things any longer.

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:07.680
Ah, speak of the devil...

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:16.400
Your father's clean break.

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:19.560
One signature?

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:26.360
There.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:32.600
Gerald will be in touch with your man.

00:16:31.680 --> 00:16:34.520
I take it it is a man?

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:37.560
Thank you for doing this...

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:38.920
I have to go.

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:43.760
We don't want any fuss, do we?

00:16:43.400 --> 00:16:48.840
Oh, and I would be grateful if you'd keep any public humiliation to a minimum.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:59.600
I really didn't want...this.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.200
You've got what you wanted, Charles.

00:17:11.640 --> 00:17:16.760
I was just wondering what you'd been telling Joseph?

00:17:16.839 --> 00:17:21.440
I asked him to stay out of it.

00:17:20.520 --> 00:17:23.720
Well, this doesn't involve him...

00:17:22.839 --> 00:17:25.240
Of course it involves him!

00:17:24.319 --> 00:17:29.600
What did you think was going to happen?

00:17:28.840 --> 00:17:32.000
All change and then as you were?

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:32.640
If we can just remain civil.

00:17:31.760 --> 00:17:32.880
Civil!

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:36.960
This is civil.

00:17:36.240 --> 00:17:39.440
This is as civil as it's going to get between you and me.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:44.520
I had hoped, after all these years, we could come to an amicable arrangement.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:47.400
You know what really upsets me about all this?

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:53.960
It's all so disgustingly ordinary and grubby and...

00:17:55.320 --> 00:18:01.560
You're not the man I thought you were.

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:04.320
I just hope you can live up to her expectations.

00:18:04.520 --> 00:18:05.800
Whoa!

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:08.600
Board room's thataway.

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:08.840
I've got...

00:18:07.920 --> 00:18:10.280
Something's happened, something important.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:10.600
Yeah.

00:18:09.720 --> 00:18:12.240
The course.

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:14.640
Path of least resistance, right?

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.720
The police called me.

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:17.640
I need to...

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.480
You have to tell them.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:19.840
Let them know.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.240
Here.

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:23.000
Car keys, car keys...

00:18:22.040 --> 00:18:23.160
Just, just tell them.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:24.840
Tell them what exactly?!

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.560
Pulse is still 130.

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:30.880
He's going into shock.

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:35.120
Give him two of O neg from the fridge.

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.040
Let's get the family out and the O neg in?

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.480
Come on, sweetheart.

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:40.120
Look, one, I'm not your sweetheart.

00:18:39.240 --> 00:18:42.240
Two, I'm not going anywhere.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:45.040
And three, if you give him O negative, you'll kill him.

00:18:44.240 --> 00:18:48.960
My brother's got antibodies to Duffy A and B.

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:49.280
He needs Duffy negative.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:49.640
Look...

00:18:48.800 --> 00:18:50.040
OK.

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:51.240
So where is this blood...?

00:18:50.560 --> 00:18:51.800
Duffy...

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:53.640
A and B negative.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:55.680
It's a black thing.

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:58.720
Liverpool.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:18:59.160
Let's get him a bed.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:02.360
Assessment complete.

00:19:03.320 --> 00:19:05.680
It's been accepted.

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:07.840
Three changes.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:13.640
My telesurgery paper for the journal.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:16.200
My father will be pleased.

00:19:16.760 --> 00:19:17.920
I've worked for this.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.280
All of it.

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:21.560
If I make consultant, I want it to be because of what I've done, what I've achieved.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:25.440
I'm a good surgeon, Joseph.

00:19:24.600 --> 00:19:29.600
I don't think that's ever been in doubt.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.040
Can we put the past behind us?

00:19:29.080 --> 00:19:30.200
Because you're a good surgeon?

00:19:29.440 --> 00:19:33.360
No, because I don't want us to be like this - constantly undermining each other.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.520
See, that's the point, isn't it?

00:19:34.640 --> 00:19:37.200
It's all about you.

00:19:36.440 --> 00:19:38.320
Your career.

00:19:37.640 --> 00:19:40.760
Whatever you do, whoever you hurt, there's only one person who counts.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.160
Listen to me.

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:45.360
I'm not the wicked stepmother.

00:19:44.560 --> 00:19:52.000
There's no magic spell, no poison apple.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:59.040
And if I'm in his bed tonight, it's because I want it and because he wants it.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:20:03.400
Don't try and come between us.

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.400
Are you threatening me?

00:20:03.520 --> 00:20:06.280
I'm telling you to grow up.

00:20:06.160 --> 00:20:10.240
We hold off transfusion as long as we can.

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:12.640
Fill him up with colloids.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:12.960
And if he doesn't stop bleeding?

00:20:12.080 --> 00:20:16.400
A little faith, and a lot of factor eight.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.080
Keep me informed?

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:20.120
Good job she spoke up for herself.

00:20:19.160 --> 00:20:20.440
Tape.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:20.800
Think that'll hold it?

00:20:19.920 --> 00:20:24.480
In Uganda, we learned how to improvise.

00:20:23.760 --> 00:20:27.240
In Holby, we do try not to.

00:20:27.120 --> 00:20:32.440
It seems to me Dr Abebe's simply thinking on her feet.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:33.360
Then in Kampala we trust?

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:38.960
Mr Prince, we will have to contact your next of kin.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:39.480
This has to stay between you and me.

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:40.400
Patient confidentiality.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:41.960
I know my rights.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.640
I'm going to go.

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:43.400
Call your wife, Geoff.

00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:43.720
No, Lalana.

00:20:43.120 --> 00:20:45.800
Wait...

00:20:45.320 --> 00:20:46.640
Hold him down.

00:20:45.680 --> 00:20:47.240
She stays.

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:47.640
Let go.

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:47.880
You!

00:20:48.480 --> 00:20:53.520
Sit...still.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:21:02.880
Sit still, you...pathetic...little...worm!

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:04.520
Better.

00:21:03.680 --> 00:21:08.080
Now you will do as I say.

00:21:07.600 --> 00:21:09.240
What are the rules?

00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.760
I do as you say, mistress.

00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:13.160
Good.

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:17.000
I'm leaving.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:30.480
Then this little slug will call the dreadful, overbearing and ungrateful Daily Mail-reading harridan he had the misfortune to marry.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:37.280
Or he'll answer to Miss Lalana.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:40.440
Mary Poppins.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:42.560
Mary Poppins, please.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:53.560
It's our safe word.

00:21:53.000 --> 00:21:54.160
I want you, not her.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:57.320
I want Mary Poppins.

00:21:56.720 --> 00:21:58.560
Eugh!

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:02.320
Right.

00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:10.280
Let's get that echocardiogram for Mary Poppins' friend here.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:15.360
Jane... his wife has a right to know.

00:22:14.480 --> 00:22:17.840
He has a right to confidentiality.

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:19.800
How would you feel?

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:22.520
We have to respect his wishes.

00:22:21.720 --> 00:22:23.320
End of story.

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.520
And if he dies?

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:28.720
We'll make sure he doesn't, won't we?

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:29.200
Mr Hope?

00:22:28.840 --> 00:22:30.320
Yes.

00:22:29.360 --> 00:22:32.840
Is this your son's phone?

00:22:32.760 --> 00:22:34.840
I don't know.

00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:36.680
They all look so similar.

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:40.360
And he always upgrades, I keep telling him not to.

00:22:40.040 --> 00:22:43.240
That's how they make their money you know?

00:22:42.440 --> 00:22:43.880
Mr Hope...

00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:48.280
Yes, er, Well, it looks familiar, but...

00:22:47.600 --> 00:22:49.440
Take your time.

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:56.000
Your mother's on her way?

00:22:55.200 --> 00:22:57.160
From Reading.

00:22:56.280 --> 00:23:01.000
She's a drug rep.

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:03.280
She'll get here as soon as she can.

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:05.280
Have we got an Hb yet?

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:08.200
Something tells me you've done this before.

00:23:07.280 --> 00:23:11.440
I've been coming here with him since I was four.

00:23:10.520 --> 00:23:12.400
Clinics, admissions.

00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:12.880
You pick up stuff.

00:23:12.120 --> 00:23:13.560
I noticed.

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:15.240
So what are you studying?

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:20.480
Biology, Chemistry and Physics.

00:23:19.600 --> 00:23:23.080
I want to go to med school, if I get the grades.

00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:24.920
I can see you put the hours in.

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:26.880
If I get a chance.

00:23:26.160 --> 00:23:28.120
He'll be fine, you know.

00:23:27.240 --> 00:23:29.880
He always is.

00:23:28.960 --> 00:23:32.600
Likes to give us all a scare.

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:35.880
I can watch him if you want to take a break?

00:23:34.920 --> 00:23:39.160
Call you if he gets more tachy, right?

00:23:38.240 --> 00:23:40.680
Right.

00:23:40.920 --> 00:23:44.880
Maybe a text, a message may look familiar?

00:23:50.080 --> 00:23:54.200
It's his.

00:23:53.320 --> 00:23:56.560
I sent him this message.

00:23:56.480 --> 00:23:58.080
It's his.

00:23:57.800 --> 00:24:01.640
In a moment, I'm going to take you inside.

00:24:00.760 --> 00:24:04.920
The body will be covered.

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:06.240
When you're ready, my colleague will show you the face.

00:24:05.360 --> 00:24:08.280
If you recognise the person, then all you have to do is tell me.

00:24:13.960 --> 00:24:17.560
Would you like some time to prepare yourself?

00:24:17.360 --> 00:24:24.680
And how would one do that, exactly?

00:24:41.520 --> 00:24:44.240
It's cold.

00:24:43.440 --> 00:24:45.360
Ready?

00:24:56.760 --> 00:24:58.000
Elliot?

00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:02.240
Elliot?

00:25:01.680 --> 00:25:03.760
No.

00:25:03.680 --> 00:25:08.360
This man is not James Hope?

00:25:07.760 --> 00:25:10.600
This boy is not my son.

00:25:22.760 --> 00:25:28.560
Diane Lloyd's replacement.

00:25:27.680 --> 00:25:33.440
Any appointment will go through the usual channels.

00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:42.200
But if word gets out that, er... there's already a local candidate who's got it in the bag, you'll find it very hard to attract serious competition.

00:25:41.240 --> 00:25:43.520
That's what I've always found.

00:25:43.240 --> 00:25:45.360
Everything will be above board.

00:25:44.480 --> 00:25:45.920
You have my assurance on that.

00:25:45.080 --> 00:25:47.840
I can ask for nothing more.

00:25:47.000 --> 00:25:50.480
I must say...

00:25:49.640 --> 00:25:52.720
Jac would complement you very well.

00:25:51.880 --> 00:25:54.880
Beauty and the Beast?

00:25:54.400 --> 00:26:02.120
I understand that, er... you're up for a merit award?

00:26:01.160 --> 00:26:05.560
At the discretion of the board, of course.

00:26:04.600 --> 00:26:06.000
Which you chair.

00:26:05.080 --> 00:26:06.280
I have that honour.

00:26:05.320 --> 00:26:12.040
And as you can imagine, the board tend to defer to me on these issues.

00:26:11.520 --> 00:26:15.560
It's the birthday dilemma, isn't it?

00:26:14.600 --> 00:26:20.360
What do you get the surgeon who has everything?

00:26:19.520 --> 00:26:24.120
You have the fast car, the perfect house.

00:26:23.240 --> 00:26:27.480
Suddenly money is no object.

00:26:26.880 --> 00:26:31.680
Tell me, this trial you're involved in.

00:26:30.800 --> 00:26:33.920
I believe there's some family connection there?

00:26:33.760 --> 00:26:35.640
My brother's wife.

00:26:35.680 --> 00:26:37.040
Of course.

00:26:36.600 --> 00:26:39.680
You were very lucky to get funding for it.

00:26:39.800 --> 00:26:47.080
What with research budgets getting ever tighter.

00:26:46.400 --> 00:26:48.120
I assume you had commercial money?

00:26:47.280 --> 00:26:48.960
Enough.

00:26:48.560 --> 00:26:55.240
But of course, the future of the trial does depend on the board's discretion.

00:26:54.840 --> 00:26:58.280
Long may it continue, eh?

00:27:02.800 --> 00:27:08.920
Shall we see what becomes of the broken hearted?

00:27:08.400 --> 00:27:11.960
Maybe I should tell Jill.

00:27:12.040 --> 00:27:15.000
You know, everything.

00:27:14.360 --> 00:27:16.080
What if something happens?

00:27:15.600 --> 00:27:17.280
You're going to be fine.

00:27:17.200 --> 00:27:19.600
Is that an order?

00:27:18.640 --> 00:27:21.400
I thought we weren't playing that game any more?

00:27:21.360 --> 00:27:24.400
There's the effusion.

00:27:23.440 --> 00:27:28.000
We are into myocardium.

00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:29.680
He needs to be in theatre.

00:27:28.760 --> 00:27:30.040
Get these tapes to Connie.

00:27:29.080 --> 00:27:37.560
She'll send as soon as she's reviewed them and you will be safe in her exquisitely manicured hands.

00:27:37.680 --> 00:27:38.920
Ah!

00:27:37.960 --> 00:27:39.200
Last but not least.

00:27:38.360 --> 00:27:42.840
Dr Derezinski.

00:27:41.960 --> 00:27:43.120
Don't try and pronounce it.

00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:45.800
Call me Miranda.

00:27:44.880 --> 00:27:46.240
Oh, and it's PhD, not MD.

00:27:45.480 --> 00:27:47.560
You must be...

00:27:46.600 --> 00:27:48.000
Dr Hope?

00:27:47.120 --> 00:27:48.520
Actually...

00:27:47.720 --> 00:27:48.840
It's not a question.

00:27:48.040 --> 00:27:50.640
Eye colour?

00:27:49.760 --> 00:27:51.800
Eye colour.

00:27:50.840 --> 00:27:52.080
Let's go, Ellie.

00:27:51.160 --> 00:27:54.560
Brown.

00:27:53.720 --> 00:27:57.920
I should have known.

00:27:57.040 --> 00:27:58.480
What do we think of that, group?

00:27:58.880 --> 00:28:00.680
I don't get it.

00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:03.120
You, Dr Hope, have just joined a minority.

00:28:03.440 --> 00:28:09.040
Sit over there with the rest of your kind and maybe you'll learn something.

00:28:10.160 --> 00:28:12.840
Bit over the top, isn't she?

00:28:12.720 --> 00:28:17.160
Blue-eyed bitch.

00:28:16.520 --> 00:28:20.200
Do you think he's going to die?

00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:21.640
He's stable.

00:28:20.680 --> 00:28:26.800
With the right operation, he's got every chance.

00:28:27.280 --> 00:28:28.640
Which means he'll come back.

00:28:28.120 --> 00:28:32.480
My regulars pay my rent.

00:28:31.640 --> 00:28:32.840
Is that all he means to you?

00:28:31.960 --> 00:28:33.960
Clients like Geoff - they get attached.

00:28:33.080 --> 00:28:38.200
They imagine things, feelings which aren't there.

00:28:37.440 --> 00:28:40.000
It's all part of the fantasy.

00:28:39.840 --> 00:28:41.040
You did nothing to discourage him.

00:28:40.160 --> 00:28:43.720
You can think what you like about me.

00:28:42.760 --> 00:28:43.920
Believe me, I am.

00:28:45.480 --> 00:28:48.480
I've said my piece.

00:28:48.440 --> 00:28:52.360
You've both got your orders.

00:28:51.440 --> 00:28:55.160
Now don't call her.

00:28:59.240 --> 00:29:03.480
Music maestro please.

00:29:02.600 --> 00:29:04.840
Colonoscopy playlist.

00:29:04.160 --> 00:29:09.040
MUSIC STARTS Bat out of Hell, good choice.

00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:09.760
You're not going to need that mask.

00:29:08.800 --> 00:29:15.320
We're working in a world of you know what down here.

00:29:15.400 --> 00:29:20.160
Shall we boldly go where no man has gone before?

00:29:19.280 --> 00:29:20.440
And the doctor is in.

00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:26.280
What concerns me is the clear conflict of interest here.

00:29:25.400 --> 00:29:26.640
Now you know the situation....

00:29:25.840 --> 00:29:29.280
I should raise merry hell?

00:29:28.400 --> 00:29:31.640
Where would that get me?

00:29:30.840 --> 00:29:34.120
Out of favour with the board and a senior colleague as an enemy.

00:29:33.240 --> 00:29:35.800
Why fight City Hall?

00:29:34.840 --> 00:29:37.040
It's the right thing to do.

00:29:36.400 --> 00:29:37.960
Because Jac Naylor's using my father to influence the appointment committee.

00:29:37.120 --> 00:29:38.280
Remind me something.

00:29:37.320 --> 00:29:41.880
Did you dump her, or did she dump you?

00:29:41.160 --> 00:29:45.760
Right, that was below the belt, wasn't it?

00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:47.000
Apologies.

00:29:46.360 --> 00:29:49.440
Everyone knows she dumped you.

00:29:48.680 --> 00:29:52.520
My concern is for my father.

00:29:51.680 --> 00:29:53.160
Then why don't you go talk to him?

00:29:55.480 --> 00:29:58.880
They're biking the blood.

00:29:57.920 --> 00:30:01.200
Three hours minimum.

00:30:00.480 --> 00:30:03.760
His heart's failing.

00:30:03.760 --> 00:30:09.320
We could risk it, hope he doesn't react to our blood.

00:30:08.520 --> 00:30:11.320
And if he does?

00:30:11.000 --> 00:30:13.880
So what now?

00:30:14.080 --> 00:30:21.240
We push in the fluids, give the Factor Eight a chance.

00:30:20.360 --> 00:30:22.000
Then wait.

00:30:21.120 --> 00:30:22.720
Mark?

00:30:21.880 --> 00:30:23.720
We wait.

00:30:30.160 --> 00:30:31.680
OK.

00:30:34.280 --> 00:30:35.800
I give up.

00:30:34.880 --> 00:30:38.480
Where are you hiding them?

00:30:39.280 --> 00:30:40.960
Open it.

00:30:44.120 --> 00:30:47.160
Ah, Mr Bond.

00:30:46.320 --> 00:30:52.240
This British ingenuity knows no bounds.

00:30:51.320 --> 00:30:52.400
Well, enjoy it while you can.

00:30:51.520 --> 00:30:55.800
It will be your last.

00:30:54.920 --> 00:30:59.480
Do you expect me to smoke, Mr Durant?

00:30:58.760 --> 00:30:59.880
No, Mr Bond.

00:30:59.000 --> 00:31:00.800
I expect you to die.

00:31:01.560 --> 00:31:06.480
She is using you just like she used me!

00:31:05.640 --> 00:31:06.920
Well, how can you be so sure of that?

00:31:06.080 --> 00:31:08.680
She was practically begging me not to support her.

00:31:07.840 --> 00:31:12.040
"I want to get this job on my own merits."

00:31:11.240 --> 00:31:13.440
Those were her exact words.

00:31:12.640 --> 00:31:14.400
Does that surprise you?

00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:14.600
No!

00:31:13.760 --> 00:31:15.200
She says what she knows you want to hear.

00:31:14.280 --> 00:31:17.800
I've done it often enough!

00:31:16.880 --> 00:31:19.840
Making me the old fool?

00:31:19.120 --> 00:31:21.000
Joseph.

00:31:20.160 --> 00:31:24.080
I support her, like I support you.

00:31:23.200 --> 00:31:25.840
You have never helped me!

00:31:25.040 --> 00:31:27.120
Not once.

00:31:26.200 --> 00:31:30.880
You had the Byrne name!

00:31:29.960 --> 00:31:34.200
But she has talent, she has guts, she has drive.

00:31:33.360 --> 00:31:37.320
You earned it, I was born with it.

00:31:36.560 --> 00:31:42.520
If this is all about that stupid complaint, then forget it.

00:31:41.680 --> 00:31:45.000
These things happen.

00:31:44.320 --> 00:31:49.480
You'll be a great surgeon, boy.

00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:50.880
I know it.

00:31:49.960 --> 00:31:51.400
You love her?

00:31:52.440 --> 00:31:53.560
Yes, I do.

00:31:52.680 --> 00:31:54.520
And I love you.

00:31:54.440 --> 00:32:01.160
And I do not believe the two positions are mutually exclusive.

00:32:07.600 --> 00:32:18.360
Emotional distress, being abused, being singled out for a biological quirk that you can do nothing about.

00:32:17.520 --> 00:32:23.920
This is how it feels every single day of your life.

00:32:23.760 --> 00:32:30.000
Say it loud, baby, I'm brown and I'm proud.

00:32:29.280 --> 00:32:34.880
Any other examples of discrimination?

00:32:34.200 --> 00:32:37.400
I want to know how you felt.

00:32:36.520 --> 00:32:41.520
Ms Elliot Hope.

00:32:40.640 --> 00:32:45.960
Consultant cardiothoracic surgeon.

00:32:45.160 --> 00:32:47.080
I can't do this...

00:32:46.160 --> 00:32:48.000
Now, don't be modest, honey, and so young!

00:32:47.160 --> 00:32:49.560
We are simply not worthy.

00:32:48.760 --> 00:32:52.360
Even a high flier like you must have experienced some form of prejudice?

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:53.280
Erm, no, not really.

00:32:52.600 --> 00:32:57.440
An attractive woman in a male-dominated culture?

00:32:56.560 --> 00:33:00.840
Actually, I slept my way to the top.

00:33:01.080 --> 00:33:05.680
Isn't that what you call positive discrimination?

00:33:05.640 --> 00:33:09.960
You just volunteered for the next exercise.

00:33:09.720 --> 00:33:12.440
They'll be landing about now.

00:33:11.920 --> 00:33:16.400
Yeah, Ibiza's not all it's cracked up to be.

00:33:15.600 --> 00:33:20.120
Just sand, sea and all the sex you can eat.

00:33:20.400 --> 00:33:21.960
So who's the stuffed blouse?

00:33:21.120 --> 00:33:24.360
Keeping her beady eye on me.

00:33:23.560 --> 00:33:31.000
You look after your regulars, Mr Durant.

00:33:31.000 --> 00:33:32.080
Most of 'em.

00:33:31.400 --> 00:33:34.240
Can't you smoke any quicker?

00:33:33.560 --> 00:33:34.800
I'm savouring it.

00:33:33.960 --> 00:33:40.120
Even a decrepit old burden like me deserves a little guilty pleasure.

00:33:39.280 --> 00:33:40.960
Burden?

00:33:40.080 --> 00:33:44.240
Their loss is our gain.

00:33:43.280 --> 00:33:46.960
What are you doing tonight?

00:33:46.200 --> 00:33:48.560
Fancy a drink?

00:33:47.600 --> 00:33:50.880
Long as it's a Pina Colada.

00:33:50.000 --> 00:33:51.720
I'm very partial to Pina Coladas.

00:33:50.840 --> 00:33:53.160
Then it's a date.

00:33:52.240 --> 00:33:53.560
Hurry up.

00:33:52.640 --> 00:33:54.000
Right, you're in luck.

00:33:55.160 --> 00:33:59.880
They had the monthly clean this morning.

00:33:59.000 --> 00:34:02.360
I'm joking...

00:34:03.200 --> 00:34:04.400
All right, suit yourself.

00:34:03.480 --> 00:34:07.000
All right, just stay here while I get help, OK?

00:34:07.800 --> 00:34:10.760
What do you mean, cancelled?

00:34:09.800 --> 00:34:13.520
I've been waiting for six months for my operation.

00:34:13.199 --> 00:34:17.159
Emergency procedures take priority.

00:34:16.199 --> 00:34:19.639
It's just a fact of life.

00:34:18.920 --> 00:34:25.679
So why is it that you have time to operate on all those blue-eyed folks at the clinic?

00:34:24.760 --> 00:34:27.120
They pay me.

00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:30.840
Everyone knows blue-eyed people take priority.

00:34:30.360 --> 00:34:34.639
Us browns just have to wait.

00:34:33.679 --> 00:34:35.600
Well, maybe I don't want to wait any more.

00:34:35.159 --> 00:34:38.400
Then it's the matter of my fee.

00:34:37.480 --> 00:34:40.440
I've got no money.

00:34:39.760 --> 00:34:41.920
Then you just have to wait.

00:34:41.560 --> 00:34:43.360
Racist.

00:34:42.679 --> 00:34:44.360
What did you call me?

00:34:44.719 --> 00:34:48.199
I said, Ms Hope, that you are a racist.

00:34:47.320 --> 00:34:50.920
That you're only refusing to operate on me because of the colour of my eyes.

00:34:51.639 --> 00:34:54.840
You want to talk about prejudice?

00:34:53.960 --> 00:34:56.400
I'll tell you about prejudice.

00:34:55.600 --> 00:35:01.480
Try growing up a brown-eyed girl in a blue-eyed family.

00:35:01.160 --> 00:35:09.120
Try working hard for something and having it snatched away just because your eyes don't fit.

00:35:08.160 --> 00:35:13.880
So I changed, I changed and I started living a lie.

00:35:13.000 --> 00:35:19.840
Because I had a dream, and this was the only way to make it come true.

00:35:22.880 --> 00:35:25.040
Contact lenses.

00:35:24.320 --> 00:35:26.120
See?

00:35:26.520 --> 00:35:28.080
Brown.

00:35:27.920 --> 00:35:29.880
Just like you.

00:35:30.040 --> 00:35:34.480
So, what do you have to say to that?

00:35:33.880 --> 00:35:36.440
You can sit down now.

00:35:37.960 --> 00:35:39.920
All right, give it to me.

00:35:40.280 --> 00:35:42.680
What happened?

00:35:41.800 --> 00:35:44.280
He was collapsed in the bog.

00:35:43.320 --> 00:35:45.800
It might be his stomach.

00:35:44.920 --> 00:35:51.200
My father has a duodenal ulcer.

00:35:50.760 --> 00:35:54.320
It may be bleeding.

00:35:54.120 --> 00:35:57.360
Give me another one!

00:35:56.480 --> 00:35:58.520
We get him scoped.

00:35:57.560 --> 00:35:59.160
It's the only way to stop the bleeding.

00:35:58.320 --> 00:36:00.920
Do you want me to have a go?

00:36:00.120 --> 00:36:01.960
No.

00:36:01.080 --> 00:36:02.360
I can manage.

00:36:01.680 --> 00:36:02.880
Donna, how long?

00:36:02.040 --> 00:36:04.800
A few minutes.

00:36:04.000 --> 00:36:08.000
He was complaining about his ulcer.

00:36:08.040 --> 00:36:11.880
I'll ring the endoscopy suite.

00:36:12.360 --> 00:36:25.040
Right, FBC, U and E's, clotting factors and six units of crossmatch.

00:36:24.200 --> 00:36:28.600
No, there's no ulcer.

00:36:30.400 --> 00:36:31.680
Feel.

00:36:30.720 --> 00:36:35.240
On the cusp, eh?

00:36:34.440 --> 00:36:38.440
One Jimmy Choo between life and death.

00:36:38.520 --> 00:36:39.600
This?

00:36:38.680 --> 00:36:42.080
We see this kind of thing all the time.

00:36:41.200 --> 00:36:44.040
Lucky you came on a quiet day.

00:36:44.400 --> 00:36:48.560
Jill doesn't deserve this.

00:36:47.760 --> 00:36:51.240
She's great, so solid, so real.

00:36:51.040 --> 00:36:54.960
God knows what she's going to say.

00:36:54.160 --> 00:36:58.720
Well, whatever it is, I think it will be better coming from you.

00:36:58.080 --> 00:37:05.040
Women don't like surprises unless they come from Tiffany's.

00:37:04.640 --> 00:37:05.720
What, you think I should talk to her?

00:37:04.800 --> 00:37:07.160
You have no-one to blame but yourself.

00:37:06.480 --> 00:37:08.480
I think he knows that, doctor.

00:37:07.520 --> 00:37:08.760
No, no, she's right.

00:37:07.880 --> 00:37:12.600
Why shouldn't she express an opinion?

00:37:11.920 --> 00:37:14.840
I like strong women.

00:37:14.000 --> 00:37:17.960
Jill is just the same.

00:37:17.040 --> 00:37:20.320
God, she deserves better than me.

00:37:19.440 --> 00:37:22.600
Better than this... constant deception.

00:37:22.240 --> 00:37:25.160
Do you think she would understand?

00:37:24.840 --> 00:37:27.200
If it came from you?

00:37:26.680 --> 00:37:29.040
I don't know.

00:37:28.160 --> 00:37:31.560
I can't, can I?

00:37:33.640 --> 00:37:34.720
Even if I wanted to.

00:37:39.760 --> 00:37:42.560
Have you been smoking?

00:37:42.240 --> 00:37:46.280
It's called holistic medicine.

00:37:46.840 --> 00:37:49.880
He's stable.

00:37:48.920 --> 00:37:50.400
Just.

00:37:49.560 --> 00:37:52.000
Theatres?

00:37:51.080 --> 00:37:52.480
Still waiting.

00:37:51.640 --> 00:37:55.160
His wife should be with him.

00:37:54.400 --> 00:37:56.720
I've made my decision.

00:37:55.760 --> 00:37:59.960
Of course, my opinion counts for nothing.

00:37:59.480 --> 00:38:03.800
When you're a member of this team, when you've earned your place, then I'll listen to you.

00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:07.080
Now, I'd appreciate it if you do as you are told.

00:38:09.240 --> 00:38:12.320
I called.

00:38:11.480 --> 00:38:15.400
The blood is still an hour away.

00:38:14.840 --> 00:38:18.720
He hasn't got an hour.

00:38:18.040 --> 00:38:22.080
And if we give him that blood?

00:38:21.200 --> 00:38:23.840
It could be fatal.

00:38:23.200 --> 00:38:26.800
And this hospital wouldn't have a leg to stand on in a court, right?

00:38:26.000 --> 00:38:27.200
Right.

00:38:30.600 --> 00:38:33.080
Give him the blood.

00:38:33.680 --> 00:38:37.640
IV Piriton.

00:38:36.760 --> 00:38:41.760
IV hydrocortisone.

00:38:40.880 --> 00:38:42.560
We do all we can.

00:38:42.480 --> 00:38:47.440
Geoff Prince, is he here?

00:38:46.640 --> 00:38:50.560
I got a call, something to do with his heart?

00:38:49.680 --> 00:38:52.520
Yeah, he's in the treatment room.

00:38:51.640 --> 00:38:54.360
That's his partner over there.

00:38:53.480 --> 00:38:57.800
She'll be able to fill you in.

00:38:58.080 --> 00:38:59.920
Well?

00:38:59.320 --> 00:39:04.880
7cm aneurysm.

00:39:04.040 --> 00:39:10.400
We've got free fluid in the paracolic gutter.

00:39:09.440 --> 00:39:10.560
And otherwise stable?

00:39:09.720 --> 00:39:10.840
For now.

00:39:09.920 --> 00:39:12.800
He's responding to the fluid bolus.

00:39:11.840 --> 00:39:17.200
Good, then we heal with steel.

00:39:16.720 --> 00:39:20.920
If he'd gone to endoscopy...

00:39:21.160 --> 00:39:23.360
There's time for the touchy-feely stuff later.

00:39:22.680 --> 00:39:24.920
Can I borrow your pen?

00:39:24.080 --> 00:39:28.040
May I have the pleasure?

00:39:35.280 --> 00:39:37.000
No.

00:39:36.320 --> 00:39:43.880
We need to get this graft in fast, otherwise we're all gonna be tugging our forelocks to the new Lord B there, so I advise you to sign.

00:39:44.400 --> 00:39:50.960
Joseph will perform this procedure.

00:39:50.080 --> 00:39:52.160
Back in the real world, sign your life over to someone who can save it.

00:39:51.320 --> 00:39:54.760
I'm competent and fully conscious.

00:39:53.920 --> 00:39:56.440
My decision is final.

00:39:55.640 --> 00:39:58.440
Joseph will operate.

00:39:57.480 --> 00:39:59.360
You know I can't.

00:39:58.400 --> 00:40:01.920
I completely concur.

00:40:01.280 --> 00:40:05.640
An simple X here will do.

00:40:05.360 --> 00:40:06.600
We don't have time for this.

00:40:05.640 --> 00:40:10.160
If you don't want Daniel, then let me do it.

00:40:09.640 --> 00:40:10.960
We have to operate now.

00:40:10.040 --> 00:40:12.160
I need to talk to Joseph, alone.

00:40:11.680 --> 00:40:13.320
Fine, come on.

00:40:12.440 --> 00:40:18.840
Let's leave them to do the heart-to-heart while it's still beating.

00:40:19.160 --> 00:40:22.800
Why?

00:40:23.400 --> 00:40:25.880
Why me?

00:40:25.600 --> 00:40:26.840
I'm in your debt.

00:40:26.760 --> 00:40:32.240
I have... taken from you and given you nothing back in return.

00:40:31.760 --> 00:40:34.400
That's not true.

00:40:33.560 --> 00:40:42.720
Oh, yes, I have assumed the Byrne name is enough to make you into a great surgeon.

00:40:42.040 --> 00:40:43.160
That is what you want, isn't it?

00:40:43.600 --> 00:40:44.760
Yes, but...

00:40:44.280 --> 00:40:47.680
Then I owe you this.

00:40:46.880 --> 00:40:55.880
This chance to show to the world what Joseph Byrne is really capable of.

00:40:55.040 --> 00:40:58.160
And risk your life?

00:40:57.320 --> 00:40:58.560
High stakes, Joseph.

00:40:57.760 --> 00:40:58.960
Do this, you can do anything.

00:40:58.000 --> 00:40:59.560
Prove it to yourself.

00:40:58.680 --> 00:40:59.960
I won't do it.

00:41:00.040 --> 00:41:04.280
Won't, or can't?

00:41:03.600 --> 00:41:04.760
Both.

00:41:03.800 --> 00:41:08.920
Either you operate on me now or I'll die in this room.

00:41:08.680 --> 00:41:11.000
It's you, you're the whore.

00:41:10.120 --> 00:41:12.600
What have you done to him?

00:41:11.720 --> 00:41:14.160
I'm leaving.

00:41:13.200 --> 00:41:16.040
You're not going anywhere.

00:41:15.160 --> 00:41:16.480
Mrs Prince...

00:41:15.560 --> 00:41:18.240
Someone call security.

00:41:18.080 --> 00:41:19.200
Quickly.

00:41:18.320 --> 00:41:19.720
You'll talk to me!

00:41:18.880 --> 00:41:20.920
Like you talk to him?

00:41:19.960 --> 00:41:22.840
Why do you think he pays me?

00:41:21.880 --> 00:41:25.160
It never occurs to you that there might be something missing.

00:41:24.280 --> 00:41:26.760
A little something you can't provide.

00:41:27.000 --> 00:41:28.200
What?

00:41:27.240 --> 00:41:29.960
Sex for cash?

00:41:29.000 --> 00:41:34.960
Cheap thrills from a £50 whore he picked up in Stokeville?

00:41:34.080 --> 00:41:37.000
£50 wouldn't even buy him a disapproving look.

00:41:36.240 --> 00:41:38.680
You want to see what Geoff spends his money on?

00:41:37.880 --> 00:41:39.960
What he hasn't got the guts to tell you?

00:41:39.120 --> 00:41:41.440
Here...take a look.

00:41:52.080 --> 00:41:57.400
Jill!

00:41:59.480 --> 00:42:02.000
You can't do this.

00:42:01.040 --> 00:42:05.720
There's clear evidence of confusion.

00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:07.080
I would have to disagree.

00:42:06.240 --> 00:42:09.280
We'd be risking his life.

00:42:08.400 --> 00:42:09.720
I concur.

00:42:08.920 --> 00:42:16.800
But at this point I don't care if this operation is done by a monkey with a Stanley knife, somebody's got to stop the bleeding.

00:42:16.080 --> 00:42:17.400
Fine, then let me do it.

00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:18.120
No, you've been vetoed already.

00:42:17.480 --> 00:42:20.680
You should have been more careful.

00:42:19.800 --> 00:42:21.160
I think you wore him out.

00:42:20.200 --> 00:42:23.440
Too much rumpy, now no pumpy.

00:42:22.760 --> 00:42:27.320
Is that supposed to be funny?

00:42:26.480 --> 00:42:29.280
Sorry, consultant humour.

00:42:28.320 --> 00:42:33.960
But we'll both be doing that soon, have 'em rolling in the aisles.

00:42:33.080 --> 00:42:34.440
As long as he lives.

00:42:33.960 --> 00:42:37.040
Are you really this cold?

00:42:36.320 --> 00:42:39.320
I prefer semi-detached.

00:42:38.520 --> 00:42:42.080
I don't like being leant on.

00:42:41.440 --> 00:42:45.240
Charlie just wants a knife he can trust.

00:42:44.320 --> 00:42:49.600
You might not care about your registration but I do.

00:42:48.640 --> 00:42:49.920
What if the GMC get involved?

00:42:49.120 --> 00:42:54.640
Go call the GMC.

00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:55.160
We'll be in there.

00:42:54.240 --> 00:42:55.600
What was the wife doing here?

00:42:54.720 --> 00:42:58.200
I'm asking myself the same question.

00:42:57.280 --> 00:42:59.680
Let's move him to theatre.

00:42:58.840 --> 00:43:00.080
Or if he stays here.

00:42:59.200 --> 00:43:01.120
Well, let's tamponade him.

00:43:00.200 --> 00:43:01.560
I need a Foley catheter.

00:43:00.680 --> 00:43:05.640
Push it through and inflate the balloon.

00:43:04.760 --> 00:43:08.080
It will buy us enough time to get him upstairs.

00:43:07.200 --> 00:43:08.360
Have you done it before?

00:43:07.440 --> 00:43:08.760
No.

00:43:07.920 --> 00:43:13.760
You want to swap places?

00:43:14.320 --> 00:43:17.840
Right.

00:43:18.320 --> 00:43:20.440
Try it again.

00:43:20.960 --> 00:43:28.280
Saline.

00:43:27.600 --> 00:43:32.680
Forceps.

00:43:32.920 --> 00:43:38.640
Well done, Dr Abebe.

00:43:39.760 --> 00:43:42.560
Want to do your little dance?

00:43:41.640 --> 00:43:44.040
Welcome to my world.

00:43:43.560 --> 00:43:47.560
So how does it feel to be operating below stairs?

00:43:46.960 --> 00:43:51.520
I have assisted on this procedure...

00:43:50.920 --> 00:43:55.240
The thought of taking a knife to him...

00:43:54.360 --> 00:43:55.560
MUSIC PLAYS Can we turn that off, please?

00:43:54.760 --> 00:43:57.600
Kill the Tip.

00:43:56.880 --> 00:44:00.080
All right, there's the sac.

00:43:59.200 --> 00:44:01.400
Looks infra-renal.

00:44:00.520 --> 00:44:02.480
One point to us.

00:44:01.520 --> 00:44:02.840
See the rupture?

00:44:02.080 --> 00:44:03.440
There.

00:44:02.560 --> 00:44:04.000
And there.

00:44:03.160 --> 00:44:06.640
Two points to God.

00:44:05.720 --> 00:44:08.400
Let's try and even things up.

00:44:09.440 --> 00:44:10.800
Feel for the neck.

00:44:09.840 --> 00:44:12.440
Of course.

00:44:12.160 --> 00:44:13.240
Blood pressure's dropping.

00:44:12.360 --> 00:44:13.480
I can't see it.

00:44:12.840 --> 00:44:15.560
Then feel.

00:44:14.600 --> 00:44:20.360
Go down to the spine.

00:44:19.400 --> 00:44:22.360
Got it?

00:44:21.480 --> 00:44:23.240
I'm not sure.

00:44:22.560 --> 00:44:24.560
Listen to me.

00:44:23.840 --> 00:44:27.400
This is not Daddy dearest.

00:44:26.440 --> 00:44:28.560
It's just a patient.

00:44:27.680 --> 00:44:30.400
Just a lump of meat.

00:44:29.760 --> 00:44:32.480
Do your job.

00:44:32.160 --> 00:44:34.560
OK.

00:44:33.760 --> 00:44:39.200
Right, I've found the renals.

00:44:41.880 --> 00:44:45.760
The equaliser.

00:44:44.800 --> 00:44:48.560
Ready for the second half?

00:44:48.800 --> 00:44:51.800
Pulse is dropping.

00:44:51.040 --> 00:44:55.280
No sign of a reaction.

00:44:54.320 --> 00:44:57.120
It would have happened by now, right?

00:45:00.040 --> 00:45:05.840
I'm checking his pulse.

00:45:07.280 --> 00:45:08.360
Sac is open.

00:45:07.400 --> 00:45:10.320
Suction.

00:45:10.960 --> 00:45:12.360
And remove.

00:45:11.680 --> 00:45:14.640
Still bleeding.

00:45:15.520 --> 00:45:23.080
Lumbar artery.

00:45:22.120 --> 00:45:23.760
Gets me every time.

00:45:22.920 --> 00:45:26.960
2-0 silk?

00:45:26.040 --> 00:45:28.760
So you must be disappointed.

00:45:29.480 --> 00:45:33.160
I'm sorry?

00:45:32.320 --> 00:45:34.680
Red, not blue.

00:45:35.120 --> 00:45:37.040
Very neat work.

00:45:36.160 --> 00:45:39.680
Sure you haven't done this before?

00:45:38.840 --> 00:45:42.240
If one sticks to sound surgical principles...

00:45:41.440 --> 00:45:47.880
One can remain utterly average.

00:45:47.720 --> 00:45:52.200
It's Jac Naylor.

00:45:51.520 --> 00:45:54.040
Checking on her investment?

00:45:53.160 --> 00:45:59.520
Or am I just a hopeless cynic?

00:45:59.480 --> 00:46:05.640
Tell her Lord Byrne's got the right man for the job.

00:46:04.800 --> 00:46:09.800
The cross clamp's gone.

00:46:08.920 --> 00:46:10.240
Suction please!

00:46:09.680 --> 00:46:11.000
I can't...

00:46:10.240 --> 00:46:14.360
More suction!

00:46:13.440 --> 00:46:17.680
Get sued by the Byrne family?!

00:46:16.840 --> 00:46:19.880
This is your mess.

00:46:19.000 --> 00:46:21.800
But, I can't...

00:46:20.880 --> 00:46:22.160
He's dying, please.

00:46:21.320 --> 00:46:22.760
We all have to sometime.

00:46:21.880 --> 00:46:25.000
Maybe I'll get his parking space.

00:46:24.120 --> 00:46:25.280
I don't know what to do.

00:46:24.320 --> 00:46:25.520
Then stop, think, choose, act.

00:46:24.680 --> 00:46:28.400
I can't.

00:46:27.440 --> 00:46:28.800
I...

00:46:27.920 --> 00:46:29.880
He's right.

00:46:28.920 --> 00:46:30.080
I can't do it.

00:46:29.160 --> 00:46:30.400
Please.

00:46:29.440 --> 00:46:30.880
Will you just...

00:46:31.720 --> 00:46:32.920
Then he dies.

00:46:31.960 --> 00:46:35.360
Think!

00:46:35.160 --> 00:46:37.680
The wooden spoon.

00:46:36.720 --> 00:46:37.840
Quickly, please.

00:46:41.680 --> 00:46:44.760
And clamp.

00:46:54.560 --> 00:46:55.600
Graft, please.

00:46:54.960 --> 00:46:56.520
Yours, I think?

00:47:02.120 --> 00:47:04.160
He's OK.

00:47:04.000 --> 00:47:06.960
They're taking him up to theatre.

00:47:06.640 --> 00:47:08.840
He's not a bad man.

00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:10.560
He's a confused man.

00:47:09.680 --> 00:47:11.520
I was confused once.

00:47:10.680 --> 00:47:12.080
But not now?

00:47:15.000 --> 00:47:19.760
I didn't realise that you were a...

00:47:21.880 --> 00:47:23.040
Thank you.

00:47:25.800 --> 00:47:29.040
Let me call you a cab.

00:47:28.080 --> 00:47:30.440
I'll walk.

00:47:29.600 --> 00:47:31.240
In those heels?

00:47:40.400 --> 00:47:45.560
You'll have to wait a while for that inheritance.

00:47:44.800 --> 00:47:49.120
Unless Ms Naylor gets there ahead of you.

00:47:48.200 --> 00:47:52.520
Oh, and for the record, I choose my own team.

00:47:51.800 --> 00:47:55.200
As long as the price is right?

00:47:54.280 --> 00:47:58.360
Consultant training lesson one.

00:47:57.520 --> 00:48:00.600
What you say and what you do are not the same thing.

00:48:00.280 --> 00:48:01.400
Ms Naylor seems to have that knack.

00:48:00.600 --> 00:48:04.160
One should lie to get ahead?

00:48:03.400 --> 00:48:04.920
Maybe she does love your old man.

00:48:04.200 --> 00:48:06.160
To me, in fact.

00:48:05.280 --> 00:48:11.600
OK.

00:48:11.280 --> 00:48:14.800
Better than God.

00:48:13.840 --> 00:48:16.600
Back pats all round.

00:48:15.840 --> 00:48:20.280
Leaking at the top end, swab!

00:48:21.680 --> 00:48:23.720
It's not working.

00:48:27.960 --> 00:48:32.440
So he gets the hugs, you get the attitude?

00:48:32.440 --> 00:48:38.760
If you want to do this job, you need a little distance.

00:48:37.960 --> 00:48:40.840
I want to be a good doctor.

00:48:40.360 --> 00:48:42.920
You will be.

00:48:43.080 --> 00:48:44.200
Come on.

00:48:44.360 --> 00:48:49.800
This girl saved his life.

00:48:52.160 --> 00:48:53.280
So?

00:48:53.320 --> 00:48:55.120
Did we pass?

00:48:54.280 --> 00:48:57.520
The incident should never have happened.

00:48:56.600 --> 00:49:01.040
I intend to deal with it.

00:49:00.560 --> 00:49:04.120
But who was the snake in the grass?

00:49:03.240 --> 00:49:05.160
Sorry?

00:49:04.520 --> 00:49:07.080
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:49:06.160 --> 00:49:07.560
Someone reported us.

00:49:06.680 --> 00:49:10.600
Anonymously perhaps.

00:49:09.800 --> 00:49:11.080
So you thought you'd take a look.

00:49:12.640 --> 00:49:13.920
I mean, stop me if I'm going wrong.

00:49:15.400 --> 00:49:18.440
That was a brave decision.

00:49:18.480 --> 00:49:24.160
We said the Q word and no-one died.

00:49:24.320 --> 00:49:29.680
I found a bed for Mrs Jolly.

00:49:28.720 --> 00:49:30.760
We are forever in your debt.

00:49:29.800 --> 00:49:33.760
Hell hath no fury...

00:49:33.480 --> 00:49:38.760
Altocalciphilia.

00:49:39.040 --> 00:49:40.480
Hmm?

00:49:39.520 --> 00:49:41.600
High heel fetish.

00:49:40.960 --> 00:49:42.160
Ah.

00:49:41.200 --> 00:49:43.600
Surprisingly common.

00:49:43.680 --> 00:49:45.160
Me?

00:49:44.280 --> 00:49:48.960
I'd have gladly walked all over him.

00:50:01.800 --> 00:50:03.480
Thank you, sister.

00:50:02.560 --> 00:50:04.200
For everything.

00:50:04.880 --> 00:50:06.040
It was you.

00:50:05.080 --> 00:50:07.440
You called her, didn't you?

00:50:13.400 --> 00:50:16.360
I'm sorry.

00:50:17.440 --> 00:50:18.960
No.

00:50:21.560 --> 00:50:23.040
No!

00:50:23.000 --> 00:50:26.280
You bloody stupid fool!

00:50:25.360 --> 00:50:27.920
Incompetent...

00:50:27.080 --> 00:50:29.960
Damn.

00:50:29.080 --> 00:50:31.640
Why now?

00:50:32.400 --> 00:50:36.960
I almost believed you there for a second.

00:50:36.040 --> 00:50:42.120
Despite everything I know about you, you almost convinced me.

00:50:41.240 --> 00:50:42.680
You were just looking after number one as usual.

00:50:42.840 --> 00:50:44.520
I don't understand.

00:50:44.040 --> 00:50:48.120
He had faith in me.

00:50:48.240 --> 00:50:49.800
It's a shame you didn't.

00:51:02.120 --> 00:51:04.600
Elliot?

00:51:04.640 --> 00:51:13.600
I was just saying how much you contributed today, to Ms Greyson.

00:51:13.440 --> 00:51:15.480
I spoke to no-one.

00:51:14.600 --> 00:51:16.960
No-one.

00:51:16.320 --> 00:51:21.080
Not Jayne Grayson and not Mrs Prince.

00:51:20.240 --> 00:51:22.040
What is it with your accusations, your comments, your...

00:51:21.160 --> 00:51:22.400
Prejudice?

00:51:22.040 --> 00:51:24.960
Don't put words into my mouth.

00:51:24.120 --> 00:51:25.560
Perfect timing.

00:51:24.680 --> 00:51:28.040
Sit down.

00:51:27.160 --> 00:51:35.200
Your fiancee was just explaining how her complaining to the CEO behind my back makes me a racist.

00:51:34.320 --> 00:51:36.440
It's fascinating stuff.

00:51:35.920 --> 00:51:38.240
It wasn't her.

00:51:37.360 --> 00:51:38.880
Oh, come on Ric, loyalty is an admirable quality, but...

00:51:38.680 --> 00:51:41.880
She didn't talk to Jayne Grayson.

00:51:41.000 --> 00:51:43.200
I did.

00:51:43.320 --> 00:51:45.560
It's my fault.

00:51:44.720 --> 00:51:47.200
I got carried away.

00:51:46.560 --> 00:51:49.680
Did you ask her to cover for you?

00:51:48.840 --> 00:51:53.360
He asked me to explain.

00:51:52.480 --> 00:51:53.560
I didn't.

00:51:52.680 --> 00:51:57.800
I understand there were extenuating circumstances.

00:51:56.960 --> 00:51:58.280
You'll re-take the course next week.

00:51:57.360 --> 00:52:01.520
I'll arrange it with Miranda.

00:52:00.640 --> 00:52:05.680
You, Dr Young, will face disciplinary proceedings.

00:52:05.280 --> 00:52:07.520
No, she won't...

00:52:06.560 --> 00:52:08.600
This is not negotiable.

00:52:07.640 --> 00:52:08.760
It wasn't her fault.

00:52:07.960 --> 00:52:09.480
I disagree.

00:52:08.560 --> 00:52:09.640
Dr Young has no excuse.

00:52:08.720 --> 00:52:11.320
This is not a game we're playing here.

00:52:10.400 --> 00:52:13.840
I have to address this complaint and be seen to address it.

00:52:13.400 --> 00:52:14.720
I'm sorry.

00:52:13.840 --> 00:52:15.800
Then I'll resign.

00:52:15.240 --> 00:52:16.480
No, Elliot.

00:52:15.520 --> 00:52:17.720
I won't accept it.

00:52:17.440 --> 00:52:25.440
There are two more parents out there right now, waiting, worrying, desperate for news.

00:52:24.560 --> 00:52:30.400
Soon they'll get a phone call, just like I did.

00:52:29.560 --> 00:52:30.680
Probably at some very inconvenient time.

00:52:29.720 --> 00:52:38.160
They're going to go down, and have to look into the eyes of that dead boy, and say yes, that's our son.

00:52:37.560 --> 00:52:42.360
And then their lives will be over.

00:52:41.640 --> 00:52:45.040
I understand.

00:52:44.200 --> 00:52:47.080
You have my sympathy.

00:52:46.320 --> 00:52:53.960
But I cannot condone what Dr Young has done.

00:52:53.280 --> 00:52:56.680
Then I refuse to take the course, at St James' or wherever.

00:52:56.640 --> 00:52:57.920
Then you leave me no choice.

00:52:57.080 --> 00:53:01.520
Both of you will have to face the board.

00:53:00.720 --> 00:53:04.720
I'm genuinely sorry it has come to this.

00:53:06.280 --> 00:53:08.240
Well, we did it.

00:53:07.360 --> 00:53:09.240
The Q word.

00:53:09.320 --> 00:53:14.040
Still, I don't think the CEO is exactly my best friend.

00:53:13.120 --> 00:53:18.840
Actually, my best friend isn't even my best friend any more.

00:53:18.680 --> 00:53:22.440
Shall we tell Mrs Jolly the good news?

00:53:21.520 --> 00:53:24.200
Margaret.

00:53:23.360 --> 00:53:25.360
Oh, no!

00:53:24.560 --> 00:53:27.600
Need some help here, please!

00:53:26.880 --> 00:53:32.200
BUZZER SOUNDS I need a crash trolley, please!

00:53:54.960 --> 00:53:56.560
It wasn't your fault, Joseph.

00:54:00.440 --> 00:54:05.160
Every operation, there are risks.

00:54:05.000 --> 00:54:06.360
Whatever we do.

00:54:05.440 --> 00:54:06.640
You know that.

00:54:05.680 --> 00:54:07.040
You have to listen.

00:54:06.080 --> 00:54:10.320
How severe, please?

00:54:09.360 --> 00:54:15.280
With the right rehab, there's every chance of a full recovery.

00:54:14.760 --> 00:54:16.680
I want you to concentrate.

00:54:15.800 --> 00:54:19.080
Squeeze as hard as you can.

00:54:21.880 --> 00:54:24.600
Try again.

00:54:25.720 --> 00:54:27.360
Again, please.

00:54:33.960 --> 00:54:35.560
It's fine.

00:54:37.160 --> 00:54:38.520
No.

00:54:37.680 --> 00:54:43.040
Not like this.

00:54:46.520 --> 00:54:49.200
You made your bed.

00:54:48.360 --> 00:54:52.120
Still want to lie in it?

00:54:52.920 --> 00:54:56.360
Pina Colada.

00:54:56.520 --> 00:54:58.680
Quiet in here tonight.

00:55:03.320 --> 00:55:05.480
Sorry mate, no smoking.

00:55:05.800 --> 00:55:07.720
Arrest me.

00:55:07.520 --> 00:55:08.640
Sorry.

00:55:12.720 --> 00:55:16.240
Want to make that two.

00:55:19.160 --> 00:55:21.360
Thought you gave that up?

00:55:21.560 --> 00:55:23.200
I did.

00:55:22.240 --> 00:55:24.920
This isn't mine.

00:55:24.640 --> 00:55:27.840
Let me guess.

00:55:27.320 --> 00:55:32.520
I shouldn't be too judgemental, you're your own man.

00:55:31.880 --> 00:55:33.400
Exactly.

00:55:32.600 --> 00:55:35.760
But angrier.

00:55:34.960 --> 00:55:36.120
I stand by what I did.

00:55:35.160 --> 00:55:41.800
Thandie deserves every chance.

00:55:41.000 --> 00:55:42.480
And not just because of me.

00:55:41.600 --> 00:55:44.640
She saved your patient.

00:55:43.760 --> 00:55:45.280
It's true.

00:55:44.560 --> 00:55:48.880
Your behaviour towards her was unacceptable.

00:55:47.920 --> 00:55:55.040
I had no choice but to let Jayne Greyson see for herself.

00:55:54.720 --> 00:55:57.480
You'll like this one.

00:55:57.080 --> 00:56:04.720
This prostitute picks up a client and as they're doing it, she can't help noticing that he's whispering.

00:56:03.920 --> 00:56:09.680
She can never quite hear what he's saying, but he keeps whispering all the time, whisper, whisper, whisper.

00:56:09.160 --> 00:56:17.040
And eventually she says, "Look, "if you're going to whisper, "at least whisper in my ear."

00:56:16.160 --> 00:56:20.920
So he leans forward, and whispers in her ear.

00:56:20.320 --> 00:56:22.000
And d'you know what he's saying?

00:56:22.320 --> 00:56:28.280
(I've only got a fiver. )

00:56:31.800 --> 00:56:38.000
We all get taken for a ride sometime.

00:56:37.840 --> 00:56:42.240
Do things we wouldn't normally do.

00:56:42.280 --> 00:56:45.520
Cover for people.

00:56:44.800 --> 00:56:49.320
Make phone calls to CEOs.

00:56:48.840 --> 00:56:53.040
The trick is to see it before it's too late.

00:56:52.600 --> 00:56:55.120
I'm getting married.

00:56:54.800 --> 00:56:56.080
That's my point.

00:56:58.040 --> 00:56:59.760
Enjoy your drink.

00:57:11.280 --> 00:57:12.720
Cheers.

00:57:11.760 --> 00:57:15.800
Bangkok?!

00:57:14.840 --> 00:57:18.600
He phoned you from Bangkok?

00:57:17.720 --> 00:57:19.680
Yes, yes.

00:57:18.920 --> 00:57:20.440
Thank you.

00:57:19.960 --> 00:57:24.960
Thank you, Becky.

00:57:24.240 --> 00:57:26.200
Yes, OK.

00:57:27.400 --> 00:57:28.960
Bye.
